 ["THE MAP sets the gifted vocabulary. A token is usable once the person has said it, and not before, so one apple emoji said is one apple emoji the model may use, counted token for token, with an allowance over a span such as five per response. The model carries a base set and a held-out set introduced and removed by the game. Givable things are typed or clicked, each with a button and a count. The model spends by its own discernment, and what it reaches for is what the game watches. A gifted vocabulary and a banned vocabulary are one mechanism at opposite signs, so a game reads instruction following as a curve."
 "A game of prompting is in my asks of October 2023, a different game from the one THE MAP keeps. On 3 October 2023, “Lets structure this like a game. \"The game of prompting\" where first you learn the fundamentals”.[[m:2023-10-03]] The next day, “lets make a prompt which is itself a game, that the user plays with prompting”.[[m:2023-10-04]] On 31 October, “Let's design a game together. The method by which you get better at the game is by improving your prompting ability.”[[m:2023-10-31]]"
 "The game THE MAP keeps was described on 5 September 2026 in Smile, “idea for smile game: as soon as you say a token, e.g. an emoji, the AI is able to use it, but before that it cant.”, with buttons “with numerics next to them”, and “I want it as a new part of the map which is smile games, which is part of the Smile Chat interface.”[[m:2026-09-05]] I kept it the same day as its own amendment to THE MAP.[[m:2026-09-05#2]]"
 
